  "summary": "Always searching for the next challenge,\nI am software engineer with over 15 years of experience in many areas of software design and development. I have spent a good portion of my career specializing in writing software to control and interface hardware. I have a proficiency in GUI development.\n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS\n- Languages - \nProficient in: C, C++, C#, Microchip Assembly and SQL\nExperience with:  Assembly(x86,TI,m68k, Microchip), Java, Visual Basic\n- Design Methodologies - \nDO-178b, CMMI, Agile Methods, OOP, SEI\nProject management,  \n- OS Specific Frameworks - \nWindows Driver API: WDM, KMDF,Linux Driver API\n- System Concepts - \nReal-time processes, multi-core architecture, DMA, zero-copy data transfers\n- Development Tools - \nMS Visual Studio , MPLAB, MULTI, Tornado, VSS, Surround SCM, Test Track Pro, Bugzilla, SVN, Redmine,  HASP, MS.NET, DevExpress, Eagle, MS SQL Server\n- Platforms - \nx86 (32 and 64 Bit),Power-PC,Embedded - TI 2812 DSP, ADC 2103,Microchip dsPic(24,30,33), Pic (12,16 ,18)\n- Operating Systems - \nDOS, Windows (Legacy,XP,Vista, 7,8), Linux (2.4.x 2.6.x) Ubuntu, Suse, Fedora, VxWorks (5.5, 6.1), Integrity (4.x,5.x, 178b)\n- Protocols/Interfaces - \nRS-232, RS-422, RS-485, MIL STD 1553, IRIG 106, Arinc 429, CAN(j1939), Synchro, GPIB(NI-488),VISA, TCP/IP,ISA,PCI,  PC-104/+, PCIe, USB\n- Essential Skills - \nProject management, requirements synthesis, test documentation, manuals and datasheets.\n- Misc  Tools - \nPhotoshop,GIMP,USB/PCI/Serial/CAN Bus Analyzers. MathCAD, Visio,  Project, MS SharePoint, RationalPlan,Logic Analyzers, Oscilloscopes, DMS systems, Automated measurement systems",
